# LOCKED: Ctrl+H must NOT hide the application

**Do not change this behavior.** User locked it after repeated regressions.

## Required behavior

- `Ctrl+H` / Screenshot = capture only. Toolbar + overlay stay visible.
- Hide/Show is **only** `Ctrl+B` (`toggle_app` / `hide_app` / `show_app`).
- Screen-share WDA / Ctrl+B cloak behavior is locked separately — see `screen-share-wda-lock.mdc`.

## Forbidden (do not reintroduce)

In `capture_interview_screenshot`, `emit_capture`, `capture_screenshot`, or `screenshot::capture_primary_for_api`:

- `stealth::hide_window` / `show_window` around capture
- `std::thread::sleep` “for compositor” before capture
- Setting `app_visible` false as part of screenshot
- Comments claiming “must hide overlay so vision doesn’t see the answer”

## Correct approach for clean screenshots

Use `stealth::protect_all_windows` / WDA exclusion. If vision still reads the overlay, fix prompting or crop — **do not hide UI**.

## If editing capture code

Keep debounce/`capture_lock` if needed. Never add hide/restore.
